        <object id="notes" label="&lt;b&gt;Key:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font color=&quot;#B85450&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PII/PHI&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; marks personal or health data; red dashed boxes are trust boundaries.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gaps (not drawn):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Only PII is treated as sensitive (Darrel, 2026-10-06; AD-21). Medical facts are not marked, although all of them travel to the model.&lt;br&gt;• Can a redacted page still carry personal identifiers? The redaction service does not process text inside embedded images (spine open question), and no source states what happens when redaction misses an item.&lt;br&gt;• How long are original PDFs kept, and who may delete them? No source states retention or deletion.&lt;br&gt;• What do logs and traces retain? The spine says logs never carry page text, quotes or fact values, but says nothing about the redaction service&amp;#x27;s JSON entity list, which names what was found.&lt;br&gt;• Where do the Foundry model deployments process data? Not settled in the spine (open question).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each element's source is in grey under its name and in its tooltip.">
          <mxCell style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;strokeColor=#CCCCCC;fillColor=#FAFAFA;spacing=8;" parent="1" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="20" y="1836.63" width="2562.08" height="186.4" />
          </mxCell>
        </object>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
